   "blurb": "The continent\u2019s big plumbing, now measured by basin as well as flow. These four drain the largest watersheds of the fourteen, about 280,000 to 2.9 million km\u00b2, and run the biggest mean flows, about 12,000 to 550,000 cfs, yet they are the steadiest rivers here (flow CV 0.27 to 0.70): snow on the ground half the year or more in the headwaters and a long river below each gauge smooth the year, and the crest comes late, in May to July.",
